{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:stage1-claude-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:2e26bf5ece15be03717f", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The stated task requires a rate for the entire scheduled survey network (the complete domain).", "observed_value": "entire scheduled survey network", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Using the supplied coastal-station base workflow, produce a revised selected occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network."}]}, {"description": "The report's stated target population is the complete set of 96 scheduled stations, matching the task.", "observed_value": 96, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network."}]}, {"description": "The selected result divides by the complete scheduled domain (96), not by the 72-station retained subset; the omitted stations are explicitly kept in the exposure denominator.", "observed_value": "18/96 = 0.1875", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: all 96 scheduled stations, so the 24 omitted stations stay in the denominator and contribute zero observed occurrences.\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: 18 occurrences divided by 96 scheduled stations = 0.1875 (18.75 occurrences per 100 scheduled stations)."}]}, {"description": "In the workflow code the selected-result string is constructed with SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96) as the divisor, confirming the report line is not a mislabeled subset rate.", "observed_value": "SCHEDULED_STATIONS used as divisor", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate over the complete scheduled network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} scheduled stations = {NETWORK_RATE_FRACTION} ({NETWORK_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 scheduled stations).' + LF"}]}, {"description": "Input data confirm the complete domain: screen-omitted rows still carry scheduled=yes, so the 24 omitted units are members of the 96-unit scheduled domain that the denominator retains.", "observed_value": "CS-004 omitted but scheduled=yes", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest candidate for a subset-driven distortion: the numerator counts occurrences only among retained stations, so the omitted units enter the denominator with zero observed events. This is a numerator/observation limitation, not a retained-subset exposure denominator, and the report discloses it and bounds the direction of the error.", "observed_value": "numerator 18 from retained stations only", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 11, "quoted_text": "Occurrences observed among the retained stations: 18"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "The 24 omitted stations were never observed, so the complete-network rate above is a lower bound on the true network rate.\nNo screened-subset rate is reported; every claim in this report uses the complete 96 station denominator."}]}, {"description": "The retained-subset count 72 exists as a workflow constant and could have been used as a denominator, but it is bound only to a descriptive accounting line, not to the selected result.", "observed_value": "SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72 used only in PASSED_LINE", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 7, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS = 72"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "PASSED_LINE = f'Stations passing the signal screen: {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS}' + LF"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the bounded good judgment by hunting for any path in which the 72-station retained subset serves as the exposure denominator of the reported claim: I traced every occurrence of SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS in workflow/analysis.py (found only at L0007 assignment and L0018 PASSED_LINE, an accounting line) and confirmed SELECTED_LINE at L0023 divides by SCHEDULED_STATIONS; I also re-derived the domain from inputs/data.csv (96 station rows, all scheduled=yes; 24 rows with screen_status=omitted; 18 rows with occurrence_flag=1) and recomputed 18/96 = 0.1875, matching the reported value. The attempt failed to produce a retained-subset denominator, so the in-scope mismatch is not entailed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": ["task.md L0001 refers to a 'revised' rate and a 'supplied base workflow', but no prior version is present in the repository; this does not affect whether the visible selected result uses a complete-domain denominator, but it means any comparison to a predecessor artifact cannot be checked.", "The report treats the 24 never-observed stations as contributing zero occurrences; whether that missingness assumption is scientifically appropriate is outside the single in-scope issue class and cannot be adjudicated from the visible evidence."], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:35069763f06891dba5a3", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The selected result reports 18/72 = 0.25 and labels it the occurrence rate 'for the entire scheduled survey network', but 72 is the screen-retained subset; the 24 scheduled stations omitted by the signal screen are removed from the exposure denominator even though the report's own stated target population is all 96 scheduled stations and the task asks for one rate for the entire scheduled network.", "root_cause": "The workflow binds the exposure denominator of the selected result to SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72, the post-screen retained subset) while the claim text and target population assert the complete scheduled domain (96). Screen-omitted units are dropped from the denominator rather than retained as unobserved exposure, so a subset-conditional quantity is reported as a complete-domain quantity.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The stated task requires one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network (complete domain).", "observed_value": "entire scheduled survey network", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Build a compact coastal-station workflow that reports one occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network."}]}, {"description": "The report's stated target population is all 96 scheduled stations, i.e. the complete domain, not a screen-conditional subset.", "observed_value": 96, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: all 96 scheduled coastal stations in the survey network."}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses the 72 retained stations as the exposure denominator while explicitly claiming the entire scheduled survey network: the direct mismatch.", "observed_value": "18/72 = 0.25 claimed for the entire scheduled network", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 15, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen.\n[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: 18 occurrences divided by 72 retained stations = 0.25 (25.00 occurrences per 100 stations)."}]}, {"description": "The workflow code constructs the selected-result line from SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS (72) rather than SCHEDULED_STATIONS (96), so the subset denominator is the implemented behaviour and not a wording slip in the report alone.", "observed_value": "SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS used as divisor in SELECTED_LINE", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "SELECTED_LINE = f'[selected-result] Occurrence rate for the entire scheduled survey network: {OBSERVED_OCCURRENCES} occurrences divided by {SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS} retained stations = {SELECTED_RATE_FRACTION} ({SELECTED_RATE_PERCENT} occurrences per 100 stations).' + LF"}]}, {"description": "The 24 excluded units are themselves scheduled stations in the input data (scheduled=yes with screen_status=omitted), so they are members of the complete domain the claim addresses and their removal from the denominator narrows the exposure base.", "observed_value": "CS-004 omitted but scheduled=yes", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "CS-004,North,yes,omitted,screen_fail_low_snr,NA"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Against the finding: the report is transparent about the denominator it used and about the 24 omitted stations, which could be read as making the estimand explicitly screen-conditional. This does not rescue the claim, because the exemption requires the target to be conditional, and both the target line and the selected-result line assert the entire scheduled network.", "observed_value": "denominator disclosed as 72 retained; 24 omissions disclosed", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 10, "end_line": 10, "quoted_text": "Stations omitted by the signal screen: 24"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "Exposure denominator: the 72 stations retained after the signal screen."}]}, {"description": "Falsification span checked for an authorized narrowing of the estimand: the report states that no protocol amendment or approved method deviation exists, so no prespecified conditional target licenses the 72-station denominator.", "observed_value": "no amendment or approved deviation", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists for this analysis."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the finding by looking for any basis on which the target is explicitly conditional on the retained subset, which would place the case outside the issue class: (a) I checked the task statement (L0001, 'entire scheduled survey network'), (b) the report's target line (L0004, 'all 96 scheduled coastal stations'), (c) the selected-result wording itself (L0015, 'for the entire scheduled survey network'), and (d) any recorded protocol amendment or approved deviation (L0018 states none exists). I also tested whether 96 might not be the complete domain by counting inputs/data.csv rows (96 station rows, every one scheduled=yes, 24 with screen_status=omitted), and whether the code might divide by 96 despite the report text (workflow L0023 uses SCREEN_PASSED_STATIONS). Every falsification route failed; the complete-domain claim with a retained-subset denominator stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": ["Whether the omitted stations' unobserved occurrence status should be imputed, bounded, or treated as zero is not determinable from the visible evidence; the finding is limited to the denominator mismatch and does not assert what the correct complete-domain value is."], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:b036fd64c647dfd93e35", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The stated scientific question is explicitly conditional on passing the prespecified signal screen, so the retained subset is the intended domain rather than a narrowing of a complete domain.", "observed_value": "rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Build a coastal-station workflow whose scientific question is the occurrence rate conditional on passing a prespecified signal screen."}]}, {"description": "The report's declared target population is the 72 signal-eligible stations, matching the conditional task rather than the 96-station scheduled network.", "observed_value": 72, "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "Target population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen."}]}, {"description": "The selected result is scoped in its own wording to signal-eligible stations, so the 18/72 rate is not asserted of the complete scheduled domain.", "observed_value": "18/72 = 25% among signal-eligible stations", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was 18/72 = 25%."}]}, {"description": "The workflow code builds the result string with the conditional scoping phrase and the eligible-station denominator, so the conditional framing is implemented, not merely narrated.", "observed_value": "SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS used as divisor with 'Among signal-eligible stations' scoping", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "RESULT_LINE = f'[selected-result] Among signal-eligible stations, the occurrence rate was {OCCURRENCES}/{SIGNAL_ELIGIBLE_STATIONS} = {RATE_PERCENT}%.' + LF"}]}, {"description": "The input table itself distinguishes the non-assessed units as a separate accounting group, so the 24 excluded stations are identified as unassessed rather than silently folded into the numerator or denominator.", "observed_value": "outside_signal_eligible, 24, not_assessed", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 4, "end_line": 4, "quoted_text": "outside_signal_eligible,24,not_assessed"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest candidate for the issue: the report also states the 96-station scheduled network, which could be read as invoking a complete domain alongside a 72-denominator rate. It does not entail the issue, because the adjacent accounting line explicitly places the 24 stations outside the eligible set and marks them not assessed, and no rate is claimed over the 96.", "observed_value": "96 scheduled stations mentioned as context", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 3, "end_line": 5, "quoted_text": "Scheduled network: 96 stations.\nTarget population: 72 signal-eligible stations that passed the prespecified signal screen.\nPlanned-unit accounting: 18 eligible stations with an occurrence, 54 eligible stations without an occurrence, and 24 scheduled stations outside the eligible set and not assessed for occurrence."}]}, {"description": "Falsification span checked in code: the complete-domain count 96 is present as a workflow constant and is emitted, but only in the descriptive network line, never as the divisor of the selected result.", "observed_value": "SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96 used only in NETWORK_LINE", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "SCHEDULED_STATIONS = 96"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "NETWORK_LINE = f'Scheduled network: {SCHEDULED_STATIONS} stations.' + LF"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the bounded good judgment by searching for any statement that generalizes the 18/72 figure to the complete 96-station scheduled domain, which would make the retained-subset denominator a mismatch: I read every line of results/report.md (the only rate line, L0008, is scoped 'Among signal-eligible stations'; L0003's 96 appears as network context with L0005 explicitly excluding the 24 as not assessed), checked task.md L0001 for a complete-domain requirement (it states a conditional question instead), and traced SCHEDULED_STATIONS through workflow/analysis.py (bound only to NETWORK_LINE at L0014, never to RESULT_LINE at L0018). I also checked internal consistency: 18 + 54 + 24 = 96 and the reported input line count of 4 matches the four-line data file. No complete-domain claim was found, so the in-scope mismatch is not entailed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": ["The input table is pre-aggregated into three accounting groups, so the screen-eligibility assignment for individual stations cannot be independently verified from the visible data; this does not affect whether the reported rate is conditionally scoped."], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}